# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# ⚠️ NOT LOAD-BEARING ANY MORE, AND NOT USED BY THE LIVE DEPLOYMENT.
#
# The live site is a RENDER STATIC SITE (see render.yaml). Render does not read
# this file — it is Cloudflare Pages syntax — and the operator has ruled out
# Cloudflare. It is kept only because `.github/workflows/deploy-cloudflare-pages.yml`
# still asserts its presence, and because the rule below is harmless and would
# still be correct if that route were ever revisited.
#
# WHAT IT USED TO BE FOR, AND WHY THAT NO LONGER APPLIES.
# `app/page.tsx` was a server component whose entire body was
# `redirect("/dashboard")`. Under `output: "export"` there is no server, so the
# root exported as `<html id="__next_error__">` — a Next.js error document —
# while the build exited 0 and printed "✓ Exporting (2/2)". This file answered
# `/` at Cloudflare's edge so that document was never reached.
#
# That is fixed at the source now: `app/page.tsx` is a real client-side
# redirect page that exports as an actual HTML document in BOTH build modes, so
# `/` is served correctly by any host. The fix had to move into the app because
# the same trick does NOT work on Render: Render does not apply redirect or
# rewrite rules to a path when a resource already exists at that path, and
# out/index.html exists. The build now asserts the root is not an error
# document, so this file is a belt beside braces rather than the only guard.
/    /dashboard    302
